## MCP tool sources

The bot opens one MCP client per source at startup and registers the server's
tools on that agent's LLM. Each address and token is read from the environment,
never written here.
{{range $a := .Agents}}{{range $a.MCPSources}}
- `{{.Name}}` on agent `{{$a.Name}}`, address from `{{.URLEnv}}`{{if .Tools}}, offering {{range $i, $t := .Tools}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}`{{$t}}`{{end}}{{else}}, offering every tool the server exposes{{end}}
{{- end}}{{end}}

Two things to expect at run time:

- **A selected name the server does not expose is never offered.** The server's
  tool list only exists once the connection is open, so nothing can check those
  names at compile time. If a tool is never called, check its spelling against
  the server's own list first.
- **An unreachable server stops the bot.** The client's `start()` raises during
  setup, so the process exits with the connection error rather than answering a
  call without the tools it promised.
{{- end}}

