Do these in the [Twilio Console](https://console.twilio.com), in this order.

1. **A voice-capable number.** Phone Numbers, Manage, Buy a number, with the
   Voice capability. Skip this if you already own the number you want. If you set
   up the LiveKit target from this repository, the same account and the same
   number serve this one, and you already own everything in action {{$trunk}} as well.
{{- if .DailyCarrier.HasInbound}}
2. **Point the number at the helper.** Phone Numbers, Manage, Active Numbers,
   your number, Configure. Set "A call comes in" to a Webhook, method POST, at
   `https://<your helper host>/call`. That host is what the tunnel command below
   prints, so run it first and paste what it gives you.
{{- end}}
{{- if or .DailyCarrier.HasOutbound .HasColdTransfer}}
{{$trunk}}. **A trunk termination address, because this agent places calls.** Elastic SIP
   Trunking, Manage, Trunks: create a trunk or reuse the one you have. On its
   Termination tab, set the Termination SIP URI to a domain ending in
   `pstn.twilio.com`. That whole domain is the value of
   `{{.DailyCarrier.SIPAddressEnv}}`. **Pick a prefix nobody could guess**, because
   action {{$acl}} authenticates callers by address rather than by password.
{{$acl}}. **Allow Daily's addresses to use that trunk.** Elastic SIP Trunking, Manage,
   Access Control Lists: create an IP access control list holding the `sip.hosts`
   entries from <https://ip-info.daily.co/ips/ip-info.json>, then attach it to the
   trunk's Termination under Authentication. There is no credential list to set
   up here and no username or password to store: Daily's outbound SIP carries no
   credentials on any documented surface, so the address list is the whole of it.
   That list changes; Daily publishes changes in the same file three days ahead.
   If termination starts rejecting calls, re-read it.
{{- end}}
{{if .DailyCarrier.HasInbound}}
Two console paths worth knowing, because moving a number between targets uses
